Gate the import to match its users, e.g. replace check.rs:207 with:

  #[cfg(feature = "dl_transitive")]
  use oxrdf::NamedNode;
  #[cfg(any(feature = "dl_transitive", feature = "dispatch_ql"))]
  use oxrdf::Term as OTerm;

Or, simpler and drift-proof, delete the import and use fully-qualified paths at the four use sites (`oxrdf::Term::NamedNode(oxrdf::NamedNode::new_unchecked(...))` at check.rs:524/527 and `oxrdf::Term::NamedNode(n)` in `ql_kb`). Then confirm all four states are warning-free: `cargo clippy -p sparq-reason-dl -- -D warnings`, `--features dispatch`, `--features dispatch_ql`, `--all-features` (add `--all-targets` to each).

Bind the base once and cfg-gate only the augmentation, e.g.:

  let mut conclusion_for_extraction = conclusion.to_vec();
  #[cfg(feature = "dl_transitive")]
  { /* premise_roles collection + declaration push into conclusion_for_extraction */ }

which keeps a single source for the base vector (mark it `#[allow(unused_mut)]` or use the cfg'd-block form if the `mut` trips a warning with the feature off).
